; s104 witness (a): the aliasing case the guard exists for. @stencil
; is the real a2 kernel's pre-midend WIR, verbatim — the shape the
; versioner versions with an overlap guard and a guard-justified
; noalias fact on the fast path. @main builds ONE container and
; passes its header as BOTH arguments (the `let b = a` header-copy
; shape; surface wolf refuses it as E1002, the c04 exclusivity
; theorem, so a hand-built module is the only place this executes —
; the s99 posture). At runtime the buffers overlap totally: the
; guard must send execution down the SLOW loop, whose feedback
; semantics (out[i] reads the out[i-1] just written) yield
; a = [0,3,8,15,24,5] from src[i]=i, len 6 — sink a[4] = 24, exit
; code 24. A disjoint-semantics build would print 12; the sink
; distinguishes. The never-versioned build must agree (X3: the slow
; loop preserves aliasing semantics; versioning changes speed only).
decl @stencil(mut ptr, mem.r0, ptr)

fn @stencil(mut ptr, mem.r0, ptr) {
